WEBVTT

1
00:00:10.656 --> 00:00:11.336
Ivy blinked.

2
00:00:12.176 --> 00:00:13.797
Her cabinmates were grinning at her.

3
00:00:13.817 --> 00:00:16.558
"I love your song!"

4
00:00:17.038 --> 00:00:17.699
Clara said.

5
00:00:17.719 --> 00:00:19.700
"It's so catchy!"

6
00:00:19.720 --> 00:00:24.962
"I can't believe you wrote it so fast," Willow said.

7
00:00:24.982 --> 00:00:27.723
"You're super talented, Ivy!"

8
00:00:29.263 --> 00:00:30.144
Ivy was stunned.

9
00:00:31.456 --> 00:00:33.698
"You mean you like it?"

10
00:00:33.718 --> 00:00:35.839
"We love it!"

11
00:00:36.199 --> 00:00:36.899
Clara said.

12
00:00:36.920 --> 00:00:39.921
"Our act will be amazing!"

13
00:00:41.242 --> 00:00:42.063
Willow beamed.

14
00:00:42.083 --> 00:00:44.664
"You really came through for us.

15
00:00:45.145 --> 00:00:48.427
Thanks! I'll start working on our dance moves."

16
00:00:48.447 --> 00:00:52.289
"Huh," Ivy thought in surprise.

17
00:00:52.309 --> 00:00:56.612
"I guess I should add songwriter to my list of talents."

18
00:00:59.020 --> 00:01:02.601
That afternoon the girls found an empty room where they could rehearse.

19
00:01:04.542 --> 00:01:06.242
Willow taught them the dance routine.

20
00:01:07.743 --> 00:01:11.724
She swirled and dipped, stomped her feet, and clapped her hands.

21
00:01:12.964 --> 00:01:14.685
Clara followed her every move.

22
00:01:16.625 --> 00:01:20.026
Ivy tried to keep up, but dancing was harder than it looked.

23
00:01:21.266 --> 00:01:23.607
She turned the wrong way and bumped into Clara.

24
00:01:23.627 --> 00:01:28.922
"Ivy, you're a little behind," Willow said.

25
00:01:28.942 --> 00:01:30.703
"Let's try that again."

26
00:01:34.405 --> 00:01:36.727
Ivy sighed as the girls started over again.

27
00:01:46.193 --> 00:01:48.975
When the song was over, the girls heard clapping.

28
00:01:49.856 --> 00:01:53.318
They turned to see Private and Penelope watching them from the doorway.

29
00:01:53.338 --> 00:01:55.960
"What a great act!"

30
00:01:56.364 --> 00:01:57.205
Penelope said.

31
00:01:57.225 --> 00:01:59.366
"I'm so proud of you!"

32
00:02:00.527 --> 00:02:01.387
Private nodded.

33
00:02:01.407 --> 00:02:04.669
"I don't know much about popular music acts.

34
00:02:05.269 --> 00:02:07.070
But that is a peppy tune.

35
00:02:07.851 --> 00:02:08.891
Keep up the hard work."

36
00:02:08.911 --> 00:02:13.454
"Wow!" Willow said.

37
00:02:13.474 --> 00:02:15.995
"Even Private likes our act.

38
00:02:16.876 --> 00:02:18.917
I know we will win the talent show."

39
00:02:20.138 --> 00:02:20.918
Clara nodded.

40
00:02:20.938 --> 00:02:23.580
"The talent show is just the start.

41
00:02:24.592 --> 00:02:27.353
We could be the world's next big pop stars!"

42
00:02:28.833 --> 00:02:29.873
Ivy rolled her eyes.

43
00:02:29.893 --> 00:02:32.914
"We're not that good."

44
00:02:34.335 --> 00:02:36.655
But a little smile crept over her face.

45
00:02:38.156 --> 00:02:40.856
She pictured an arena with the three of them onstage.

46
00:02:41.657 --> 00:02:42.597
Lights blazed.

47
00:02:43.417 --> 00:02:46.658
A huge crowd clapped and cheered for the songs that she wrote.

48
00:02:46.678 --> 00:02:50.579
"I could be rich one day," Ivy thought.

49
00:02:50.599 --> 00:02:53.940
"I could buy all the art supplies I wanted.

50
00:02:55.220 --> 00:03:00.744
I could even have my own art studio, and—" "Let's keep rehearsing," Willow said.

51
00:03:01.444 --> 00:03:04.186
Willow's voice had snapped Ivy out of her daydream.

52
00:03:04.206 --> 00:03:07.549
"Every step needs to be perfect.

53
00:03:08.029 --> 00:03:08.709
Right, Ivy?"

54
00:03:09.450 --> 00:03:10.591
Willow was looking at her.

55
00:03:11.691 --> 00:03:12.332
Ivy nodded.

56
00:03:12.352 --> 00:03:14.614
"Right. Let's do it!"

57
00:03:17.375 --> 00:03:20.818
The next day Ivy left the assembly hall with Clara and Willow.

58
00:03:22.019 --> 00:03:23.700
They planned to rehearse all morning.

59
00:03:24.764 --> 00:03:26.665
Then Ivy saw Ezra by himself.

60
00:03:27.565 --> 00:03:28.465
He looked upset.

61
00:03:28.485 --> 00:03:31.546
"I'll be right back," Ivy said.

62
00:03:33.426 --> 00:03:34.827
She hurried over to Ezra.

63
00:03:34.847 --> 00:03:36.647
"Where's Glen?

64
00:03:37.388 --> 00:03:39.528
Shouldn't you two be working on your act with Wes?"

65
00:03:40.768 --> 00:03:41.549
Ezra frowned.

66
00:03:41.569 --> 00:03:44.489
"Glen has been acting so weird.

67
00:03:45.650 --> 00:03:48.671
He says he can't participate in the talent show anymore.

68
00:03:49.811 --> 00:03:53.252
He's too busy being Camp Evergreen's number-one leader.

69
00:03:54.468 --> 00:03:57.469
So I guess Wes and I have to do the act without him."

70
00:03:58.950 --> 00:04:00.531
Ivy tried to cheer up Ezra.

71
00:04:00.551 --> 00:04:03.912
"Maybe that will be better," she joked.

72
00:04:03.932 --> 00:04:09.775
"Better than getting booed offstage because of Glen's terrible knock-knock jokes!"

73
00:04:09.795 --> 00:04:13.316
"It's not better, Ivy!

74
00:04:14.157 --> 00:04:15.737
Wes hardly ever speaks!

75
00:04:16.978 --> 00:04:19.259
How can we do a comedy act together?"

76
00:04:20.419 --> 00:04:21.380
Ezra hung his head.

77
00:04:22.192 --> 00:04:24.734
"I might be able to write a few jokes.

78
00:04:25.555 --> 00:04:27.757
But I can't get onstage without Glen.

79
00:04:29.018 --> 00:04:30.179
I'm too nervous.

80
00:04:31.140 --> 00:04:32.461
I don't know what to do."

81
00:04:32.481 --> 00:04:35.864
"Talk to Glen again," she said.

82
00:04:35.884 --> 00:04:38.186
"Ask him to write the comedy act."

83
00:04:38.206 --> 00:04:42.009
"You don't get it," Ezra said.

84
00:04:42.029 --> 00:04:45.953
"He—" The PA system crackled loudly.

85
00:04:46.753 --> 00:04:49.376
Then a familiar voice blared through the speakers.

86
00:04:50.624 --> 00:04:51.826
"Greetings, campers.

87
00:04:52.787 --> 00:04:54.088
It's your lucky day.

88
00:04:54.849 --> 00:05:03.299
Today's hike will be led by me—Glen, Camp Evergreen's amazing, fantastic, number-one leader.

89
00:05:04.661 --> 00:05:08.205
My assistant Larry and I will meet you in the square in ten minutes.

90
00:05:09.266 --> 00:05:10.007
Don't be late."
